title: Counting down
mode: vhdl
chapter: Counting
check: behaves
cycles: 150
random: rst=0.05
---- intro
Count backwards: 15, 14, ... 1, 0, and round to 15 again. `count - 1` works like `count + 1`, and 0 − 1 wraps round to 15.

This one has a reset too, but a reset to **9**, so it can count down from 9 like a timer: `to_unsigned(9, 4)` is the number 9 in 4 bits.
---- task
Count down by one at each rising edge; when `rst` is 1, go to 9 instead. `q` is the count.
---- start
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;
use ieee.numeric_std.all;

entity down is
  port(
    clk : in  std_logic;
    rst : in  std_logic;
    q   : out std_logic_vector(3 downto 0)
  );
end down;

architecture rtl of down is
    signal count : unsigned(3 downto 0) := (others => '0');
begin
    -- write it here
end rtl;
---- answer
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;
use ieee.numeric_std.all;

entity down is
  port(
    clk : in  std_logic;
    rst : in  std_logic;
    q   : out std_logic_vector(3 downto 0)
  );
end down;

architecture rtl of down is
    signal count : unsigned(3 downto 0) := (others => '0');
begin
    process (clk)
    begin
        if rising_edge(clk) then
            if rst = '1' then
                count <= to_unsigned(9, 4);
            else
                count <= count - 1;
            end if;
        end if;
    end process;
    q <= std_logic_vector(count);
end rtl;
---- hint1
The counter with a reset, using `- 1` and `to_unsigned(9, 4)`.
---- hint2
`if rst = '1' then count <= to_unsigned(9, 4); else count <= count - 1; end if;`
---- solution
```
process (clk)
begin
    if rising_edge(clk) then
        if rst = '1' then
            count <= to_unsigned(9, 4);
        else
            count <= count - 1;
        end if;
    end if;
end process;
q <= std_logic_vector(count);
```
---- done
A microwave timer counts down like this, and stops when it reaches zero. Next: a counter that goes round early.
